00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:04.350
but how did you choose
the title of your album,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.487
you know, "I've Tried
Everything But Therapy,

00:02:06.487 --> 00:02:09.240
"Part One," but I just,
well one, I'm gonna ask you

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:10.740
have you ever really tried therapy?

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.870
But two, I kinda love that
it's the title of the album

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:15.510
because I feel like it is
therapeutic what we do naturally.

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.100
- Yeah, absolutely, I mean
it's therapeutic for me

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.110
in a lot of ways, but I think too

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:21.480
it was something where I wanted
to start the conversation

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.430
with myself 'cause I think like

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:25.590
this generation probably
is like the first people

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.080
that are like normalizing just
talking about mental health

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.690
at all and getting the
conversation going at all

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.150
because I feel like some
weird generational like

00:02:35.384 --> 00:02:37.237
some mindset where it was like,
"I'm not going to therapy.

00:02:37.237 --> 00:02:40.297
"I'm not crazy. I don't need
that," or, "I know what's

00:02:40.297 --> 00:02:42.480
"wrong with me," you know,
and I feel like we just-

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.760
- Or in my world it was
like talk to your preacher.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:45.593
- Yeah, yeah, absolutely.

00:02:45.593 --> 00:02:47.490
- And it's like well that
can be helpful, definitely,

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:49.980
but like you know also,
people that are trained

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.080
in another version in another
way to give you tools.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.030
- And so I think just having that,

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:56.400
and if I start that conversation
hopefully maybe it'll

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.740
inspire somebody else to
have that conversation

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.570
